    "prompt": "The square $FGHI$ has area 80. Points $J, K, L, M$ are marked on the sides of the square so that $FK = GL = HM = IJ$ and $FK = 3KG$. What is the area of the shaded region?",
    "image": "qimages/ukmt/pink-2015/q11.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "40"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "35"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "30"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "25"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "20"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Shaded area is half of JKLM",
        "body": "Let $FK=3l$ and $KG=l$ so the side is $4l$ with $16l^2=80$, giving $l^2=5$. Then $FJ=GK=l$ and $JK^2=l^2+(3l)^2=10l^2=50$. $JKLM$ is a square of area 50, and the shaded region is half of it: 25.\n\n**Answer: (D) 25**"
      }
    ],
