    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "The figure shows seven regions enclosed by three circles. We call two regions neighbouring if their boundaries have more than one common point. In each region a number is written. The number in any region is equal to the sum of the numbers of its neighbouring regions. Two of the numbers are shown. What number is written in the central region?",
    "image": "qimages/ukmt/pink-2015/q17.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$-6$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "6"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$-3$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "3"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "0"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "E",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Set up equations",
        "body": "Let the central number be $x$. It equals the sum of its three neighbours, which include 1 and 2, so the third (lower) region holds $x-3$. Its neighbours then give the other regions $x-1$ and $x-2$. The lower middle region $x-3$ equals the sum of its neighbours: $x+(x-1)+(x-2)=3x-3$. So $x-3=3x-3$, giving $x=0$.\n\n**Answer: (E) 0**"
      }
    ],
